# Backlog / tracker (this repo)

Follow [`backlog/board.md`](backlog/board.md) and [`docs/PROCESS.md`](docs/PROCESS.md). Product notes in [`docs/BACKLOG.md`](docs/BACKLOG.md) remain background; PROCESS wins on conflict. Summary:

- Living board: [`backlog/board.md`](backlog/board.md); items in
  `backlog/items/ITEM-XXX-slug.md` (from `backlog/items/_template.md`).
- IDs: `ITEM-<nnn>` (consecutive; legacy `BL-*` migrated per ADR 0001).
- Statuses: `backlog` → `speccing` → `ready` → `in-progress` → `in-review` →
  `done`. Backlog column sorted P0–P3.
- WHEN an item’s status changes, update **both** the item file and the board.
- Specs stay the intent source; backlog is “what we might do”.
- Prefer linking planned product / non-trivial work to an `ITEM-*` item.
- Docs-native only — do not add backlog SaaS toolchains without asking.
